  "limitations": [
    "This is a source-association review of three selected tables, not verified corporate identity, current support entitlement, production use, compromise or customer-data exposure.",
    "The native route requires an eligible exact company label, explicit native Hong Kong country, and the canonical tenant-to-support-organization-to-ticket references. No eligible native Hong Kong attribution is inferred from organization names alone.",
    "The exact organization-name route has no inherited Hong Kong geography and establishes no native tenant, financial, cluster or gateway relationship. Existing label strings can denote aliases or different legal entities.",
    "Routes overlap and must not be added. Organization and ticket IDs are deduplicated within each route; source row observations and distinct IDs remain separate.",
    "Only equality of retained structured projections is used to collapse duplicate IDs; whole-record equality is not claimed. Conflicting projections, ambiguous mappings and explicit or unsupported deletion states are excluded.",
    "Nonnegative JSON integer identifiers are converted to decimal strings. String tokens remain unchanged; floating-point values, booleans, whitespace-padded tokens and unsupported types are rejected. No case or leading-zero normalization is applied.",
    "A missing deletion indicator does not prove that a record is active. Distinct ticket IDs are not collapsed using merge-reference metadata.",
    "Structured-field counts indicate that values or flags occur in support records. Cluster names, versions, ticket text, personal fields and raw identifiers are not disclosed; a production-down flag is not independent verification of an incident.",
    "The reviewed string Swire Properties Inc., if present, must not be substituted for a Hong Kong legal entity. Earlier reviewed identity limitations remain applicable."
  ]
